INT. ABANDONED SKATING RINK - DAWN

A vast hall with a cracked ice surface, half-melted and gray. Bleachers stripped bare. A scoreboard dangles by one chain. Pale light pours through a hole in the roof, striking the center of the rink like a spotlight.

COACH IGNATIUS PRZYBYLSKI, 60s, bundled in a parka, sits on a bucket at the boards, holding a stopwatch in mittened hands. His breath rises in plumes. On the ice, DARIUS "THE WALL" FONTENOT, 30s, a goalie with a dented mask, stands in a crouch at the net, a puck at his feet. A radio on the boards crackles.

RADIO ANNOUNCER (V.O.)
(over radio)
And that's the final from Calgary, folks. Eagles take it six to two.

COACH IGNATIUS
(turning it down)
Six to two. Hear that, Darius?

DARIUS
I heard it.

COACH IGNATIUS
That's us, in three weeks, if you do not fix your glove side.

DARIUS
My glove side is fine.

COACH IGNATIUS
Your glove side is a screen door.

Darius takes the puck and flicks it into the net. Coach shakes his head.

A figure enters from the locker-room tunnel: LENNOX "LEN" AKINTOLA-BRADY, 20s, a rookie in a too-big jersey, skates tied around his neck. He stops at the boards, intimidated.

LEN
Coach? Am I late?

COACH IGNATIUS
You are early, which is worse. It means you didn't sleep.

LEN
I slept.

COACH IGNATIUS
You slept badly.

Len sits, ties a skate. Darius watches from the net. Coach clicks the stopwatch.

COACH IGNATIUS (CONT'D)
Len, shoot on Darius.

LEN
Me? On him?

COACH IGNATIUS
You see anyone else?

Len steps on the ice. Skates a slow circle. Darius lowers his mask. Len winds up, shoots. Darius flicks the glove. The puck hits it and drops. Len stares.

DARIUS
(muttering)
Screen door.

LEN
Sorry?

DARIUS
Nothing.

Len shoots again. Darius makes the save with his pad. Coach scribbles. Len shoots again. This time the puck sails over the glove.

COACH IGNATIUS
Again.

LEN ^
Again?

DARIUS
Again.

They say it at once, a little too loudly. Coach covers a smile.

Len shoots. Darius lunges. The puck clangs off the post. The radio crackles.

RADIO ANNOUNCER (V.O.)
(over radio)
We now return to our regular programming.

Coach clicks the radio off. Quiet. Len and Darius stand facing each other.

COACH IGNATIUS
Good. Again.
